*** PRESERVED FAILING DRY-RUN -- the gate was NOT frozen on this. ***
Two DETECTOR defects, both found before any solver ran and before any threshold was frozen. Neither
is a threshold problem and neither was fixed by moving a number:

1. rarefaction tail: 102.3 dx error, and the fan measured 147 cells against an exact 44.5.
   fan_extent() selected every cell differing from BOTH plateaus by >1% of the drop. The star-RIGHT
   region (rho = 0.2656, between the contact and the shock) differs from rho_L = 1.0 and from
   rho*_L = 0.4263 as well, so it was swept into the fan. The detector had no notion of WHERE the
   fan is allowed to be.
   FIX: confine the fan search to x < the DETECTED contact position, and define head/tail as
   departure from rho_L and arrival at rho*_L rather than "differs from both".

2. V4: the shock detector returned a position of 0.91755538 on a smooth monotone ramp with NO jump.
   crossing_position() looked only for the 50% crossing, which a monotone ramp of course has. The
   detector could not tell a discontinuity from a slope, so every Group X criterion would have been
   measurable on a profile containing no shock at all.
   FIX: require the 10%->90% transition to complete within nx/5 cells, so a feature that takes a
   fifth of the domain to transition is not reported as a jump.

This is what CLAUDE.md section 5.2 is for. Had the gate been frozen first and the detectors written
afterwards, criterion X4 would have failed on a perfectly correct solver and V4 would have passed
vacuously.

